<!--
  NavigateToPose with an explicit, ordered recovery sequence.

  Structure:

    RecoveryNode (6 retries)
     |- PipelineSequence "NavigateWithReplanning"   <- the normal path
     |   |- RateController 1 Hz -> ComputePathToPose (with its own recovery)
     |   \- FollowPath (with its own recovery)
     \- ReactiveFallback "RecoveryFallback"          <- runs only on failure
         |- GoalUpdated                              <- bail out if a new goal arrived
         \- RoundRobin "RecoveryActions"

  THE RECOVERY ORDER IS THE DESIGN. Actions are ordered cheapest-and-least-
  disruptive first, and each one addresses a different cause of failure:

    1. ClearLocalCostmap   Cheapest possible. Fixes the most common cause by
                           far: a stale obstacle left in the local costmap by a
                           person who has already walked away, or a smear left
                           by a momentary localisation jump between racking
                           bays. Costs nothing and does not move the robot.

    2. ClearGlobalCostmap  Same idea one level up, for when the global planner
                           has convinced itself the aisle is blocked. Separated
                           from step 1 rather than combined because clearing the
                           global costmap discards genuine knowledge about
                           obstacles outside sensor range, so it is worth trying
                           the local clear on its own first.

    3. Spin (90 deg)       First action that moves. A 90 degree rotation sweeps
                           the 2D LiDAR across space the robot has been
                           ignoring and re-observes the aisle from a new angle,
                           which both refills the costmap and — because the
                           racking bays alias — gives AMCL a genuinely new
                           measurement to work with. Not a full 360: in a 2.8 m
                           aisle a full spin costs several seconds and the
                           second half of it observes nothing the first half
                           did not.

    4. BackUp (0.30 m)     For the case the spin cannot fix: the robot is
                           already inside the inflation band, or nose-first into
                           a pallet, so no forward trajectory scores. Backing up
                           restores room to manoeuvre. Deliberately after the
                           spin because reversing is blind — there is no
                           rear-facing sensor coverage below the 2D LiDAR plane.

    5. Wait (5 s)          Last resort, and the right answer more often than it
                           looks. If the aisle is blocked by a person or a
                           forklift, every other recovery is noise and the
                           blockage clears on its own. Waiting is also the only
                           recovery that cannot make the situation worse.

  RoundRobin, not Sequence: each failure runs the *next* action rather than
  replaying the whole list from the start. Six retries therefore walk through
  all five actions and return to the local costmap clear once, rather than
  clearing the local costmap six times.

  The ReactiveFallback wrapper around GoalUpdated aborts recovery immediately if
  a new goal arrives, so a robot mid-spin does not finish spinning before
  accepting new work.
-->
<root BTCPP_format="4" main_tree_to_execute="MainTree">
  <BehaviorTree ID="MainTree">
    <RecoveryNode number_of_retries="6" name="NavigateRecovery">

      <PipelineSequence name="NavigateWithReplanning">
        <!-- Replan at 1 Hz. Faster gains nothing: the global costmap only
             updates at 1 Hz, so a 5 Hz replan repeats the same computation
             against identical input. -->
        <RateController hz="1.0">
          <RecoveryNode number_of_retries="1" name="ComputePathToPose">
            <ComputePathToPose goal="{goal}" path="{path}" planner_id="GridBased"/>
            <ClearEntireCostmap name="ClearGlobalCostmap-Context"
                                service_name="global_costmap/clear_entirely_global_costmap"/>
          </RecoveryNode>
        </RateController>

        <RecoveryNode number_of_retries="1" name="FollowPath">
          <FollowPath path="{path}" controller_id="FollowPath"/>
          <ClearEntireCostmap name="ClearLocalCostmap-Context"
                              service_name="local_costmap/clear_entirely_local_costmap"/>
        </RecoveryNode>
      </PipelineSequence>

      <ReactiveFallback name="RecoveryFallback">
        <GoalUpdated/>
        <RoundRobin name="RecoveryActions">
          <ClearEntireCostmap name="ClearLocalCostmap-Recovery"
                              service_name="local_costmap/clear_entirely_local_costmap"/>
          <ClearEntireCostmap name="ClearGlobalCostmap-Recovery"
                              service_name="global_costmap/clear_entirely_global_costmap"/>
          <Spin spin_dist="1.57"/>
          <BackUp backup_dist="0.30" backup_speed="0.05"/>
          <Wait wait_duration="5"/>
        </RoundRobin>
      </ReactiveFallback>

    </RecoveryNode>
  </BehaviorTree>
</root>
